      {
        "id": 105277,
        "name": "McBehrer",
        "username": "McBehrer",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mcbehrer/{size}/1850_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-05-28T16:07:28.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I would say no, as Legacy is not actually being dealt damage. On the other hand, if Legacy would be dealt 1 damage, and fortitude reduces it by 1, mitigate would still trigger. Because being immune prevents the damage alltogether, and preventing functions differently than taking it. It's like with Fright Train and Hippocratic oath; preventing the damage that would be dealt to Fright Train does not cause the first-time-each-turn damage buff to be used up, but reducing it to 0 (like with the environment or something) would.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>That's my interpretation, anyway. Not official by any means.</p>",
        "post_number": 3,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:34:50.152Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
